Context
  Asked to note the testing process in CONTRIBUTING.md and add a Makefile entry
  for `claude --plugin-dir'. The flag was verified against `claude --help' before
  being written into a target: it takes a directory or a .zip and is repeatable.

Considerations
  - The four layers are ordered by what each can rule out, not by convenience.
    `checks' cannot see a path bug; `try' cannot either, because the cwd is still
    this repo; only `try-in' can. `ship-check' answers a different question again
    -- not "does it work" but "does the user receive it".
  - `ship-check' reports executables-shipped as a yes/no line rather than just
    listing files, so the answer does not depend on the reader noticing an
    absence. Today it prints NO. When the bin/ -> scripts/ move lands it should
    print YES, which makes it the regression test for that change.
  - The corpus section names the two silent things to check per project rather
    than describing a happy path, matching how the skills themselves are written.

Deviations
  - `try' and `try-in' launch an interactive session, so they are not run by CI
    and were not run here; only `ship-check' was exercised. The targets' shell is
    syntax-valid and `gmake -s help' lists all three.
